  "summary": "The previous proposal's 'single chokepoint' claim is incomplete: `run_ideating()` (phases.py:721) bypasses `_run_phase()` entirely, calling `runner.headless()` directly in a loop (lines 806, 849), so adding a log call only in `_run_phase()` would miss all ideation rounds and synthesis — a significant gap since ideation is a multi-round phase that users would especially want visibility into. Additionally, the proposal only logs after phase completion, but `runner.headless()` can run for several minutes; the web UI polls every 5 seconds (client.html:479) and would show nothing during active processing, undermining the real-time monitoring value of the log panel. A more complete fix should: (1) log phase *start* events (not just completions) so the web UI immediately reflects that work is underway, (2) add log calls in `run_ideating()` for each debate round and synthesis, and (3) include the feature slug in log entries since the web UI renders all logs in a single flat list (client.html:1431-1435) with no feature grouping, making it impossible to tell which feature a log entry belongs to when multiple items are in-flight."
